WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.675
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:16.494
Unit thirty-eight: Relative Clauses with Prepositions and Quantifiers. Today you will use formal relative structures.

4
00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:19.469
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:23.980
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:25.667
In which.

7
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:29.008
In which means a preposition before which.

8
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.454
The house in which I was born.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.389
Your turn. Say: In which.

10
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.130
In which.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.629
To whom.

12
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:42.802
To whom means a preposition before whom.

13
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:44.929
The person to whom I spoke.

14
00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:47.914
Your turn. Say: To whom.

15
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.408
To whom.

16
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.256
Some of which.

17
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.399
Some of which means a quantifier + relative pronoun.

18
00:00:57.983 --> 00:00:59.669
Books, some of which are rare.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.796
Your turn. Say: Some of which.

20
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:06.878
Some of which.

21
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:08.687
None of whom.

22
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:12.054
None of whom means a quantifier for people.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.185
Guests, none of whom came.

24
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.749
Your turn. Say: None of whom.

25
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.613
None of whom.

26
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.398
Many of whom.

27
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.836
Many of whom means a quantifier for people.

28
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.426
Students, many of whom travel.

29
00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:32.448
Your turn. Say: Many of whom.

30
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.359
Many of whom.

31
00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:38.222
The way in which.

32
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:41.994
The way in which means a relative phrase for manner.

33
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:44.107
The way in which he works.

34
00:01:44.717 --> 00:01:47.485
Your turn. Say: The way in which.

35
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.648
The way in which.

36
00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:53.303
Whose.

37
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:56.084
Whose means shows possession.

38
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.625
A man whose car broke down.

39
00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:01.265
Your turn. Say: Whose.

40
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:04.962
Whose.

41
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:06.497
Formal.

42
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:09.564
Formal means serious in style.

43
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.581
A formal style.

44
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:14.511
Your turn. Say: Formal.

45
00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.147
Formal.

46
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:22.828
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.683 --> 00:02:28.112
Visal, combine: He has ten cousins. Six of them live abroad.

48
00:02:29.217 --> 00:02:37.488
He has ten cousins, six of whom live abroad. After a quantifier we use of whom for people and of which for things.

49
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.188
How do prepositions work?

50
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:54.585
In formal English a preposition can come before the relative pronoun: The house in which I was born is old. The person to whom I spoke was kind. We use whom and which, never that, after a preposition.

51
00:02:55.683 --> 00:02:57.625
Is it always necessary?

52
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:12.381
No. In speech we say The person I spoke to. But in formal writing the preposition goes first. Remember the commas for non-defining clauses: The books, some of which are rare, are valuable.

53
00:03:13.533 --> 00:03:15.254
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.117 --> 00:03:21.657
Grammar focus: Relative clauses: preposition and quantifier plus which and whom.

55
00:03:21.957 --> 00:03:23.249
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.891
The house in which I was born is old.

57
00:03:26.783 --> 00:03:29.352
He has ten cousins, six of whom live abroad.

58
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.935
The books, some of which are rare, are valuable.

59
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:41.094
Preposition + which / whom (never that). Quantifier + of which / of whom. The clause is often non-defining, so use commas.

60
00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:45.222
Be careful! Don't say: The man to that I spoke.

61
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.143
Say: The man to whom I spoke.

62
00:03:49.443 --> 00:03:50.363
Use whom.

63
00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.680
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.851
Formal Relatives.

65
00:03:56.151 --> 00:03:59.242
The house in which I was born is more than a hundred years old.

66
00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:02.593
The person to whom I spoke was very kind.

67
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.308
She has three sisters, two of whom are doctors.

68
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.776
The books, some of which are rare, are valuable.

69
00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.579
This formal style is common in written English.

70
00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:18.552
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:21.335
The house blank I was born is old.

72
00:04:21.635 --> 00:04:25.137
A, in which. B, where which. C, that in.

73
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.607
The answer is A: in which.

74
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.678
She has three sisters, two of blank are doctors.

75
00:04:34.978 --> 00:04:37.807
A, whom. B, who. C, which.

76
00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.308
The answer is A: whom.

77
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.390
The books, blank of which are rare, cost a lot.

78
00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.600
A, some. B, those. C, any.

79
00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.131
The answer is A: some.

80
00:04:57.283 --> 00:04:58.459
Which is correct?

81
00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:04.095
A, the man to that I spoke. B, the man to whom I spoke. C, the man whom to I spoke.

82
00:05:07.633 --> 00:05:10.411
The answer is B: the man to whom I spoke.

83
00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.548
According to the reading, how old is the house?

84
00:05:14.848 --> 00:05:19.395
A, over a hundred years. B, ten years. C, fifty years.

85
00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:25.595
The answer is A: over a hundred years.

86
00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.462
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:31.317 --> 00:05:36.491
Combine: 'He has ten cousins. Six of them live abroad.' using 'of whom'.

88
00:05:45.283 --> 00:05:46.679
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:56.447
He has ten cousins, six of whom live abroad. I use six of whom to join the two sentences, and I add commas because the clause gives extra information.

90
00:05:56.747 --> 00:05:58.479
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.383 --> 00:06:06.308
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clauses: preposition and quantifier plus which and whom.

92
00:06:06.608 --> 00:06:11.699
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:15.139
See you in Unit thirty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:18.729
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

